        "invalid": 65535,
        "invalidFrom": 4095,
        "note": "12 bit, 0.5 Nm per bit, 0 Nm at raw 2047 (negative = engine braking), 4095 = no value. With factor 1 a running engine read as ~2047 Nm."
      },
      "tyreTemp": {
        "factor": 1,
        "offset": -40,
        "invalid": 65535,
        "note": "degrees + 40, in the car's temperature unit (deg F on a car set to Fahrenheit: main.js converts it): a G05 PHEV sent raw 53-57 on a ~10 deg C day (2.8.0 log), not deci-Kelvin. Values outside -40..150 deg C are shown as no data; the raw values go to the log ('raw tyre temperature')"
      },
      "tyrePress": {
        "factor": 0.1,
        "offset": 0,
        "invalidFrom": 65532,
        "note": "0.1 per bit in the car's pressure unit (bar / kPa / psi, from Vehicle.statusNewCurrentUnitsStatusExt; main.js converts it to bar). BMW x_call: raw * 0.1, valid up to 530; a car in bar sent raw 22-25 = 2.2-2.5 bar, a car in psi about 410 = 41 psi. Read as 0.1 kPa before, every tyre came out at 0.02 bar and was hidden."
      },
      "sportPct": {
        "factor": 1,
        "offset": 0,
        "invalid": 255,
        "note": "sport display power / torque in % of the car maximum; calibrate if the raw value is not 0-100"
      },
      "batteryTemp": {
        "factor": 1,
        "offset": -50,
        "invalid": 255,
        "comment": "Efficiencytainment2.statusBatteryTemperature (X5 45e: raw 76 with the cells at ~26 C)"
      },
      "yaw": {
        "factor": 0.005,
        "offset": -163.84,
        "invalid": 65535,
        "note": "deg/s; the factor and offset of the car's CAN yaw-rate signal, not yet confirmed on this field: the raw values show on Cluster Layouts' Signals page and go to the log ('raw statusYawVelocityVehicle')"
      },
      "steer": {
        "factor": 0.04395,
        "offset": 0,
        "signed16": true,
        "invalid": 32767,
        "note": "degrees at the wheel, negative to the right as BMW counts; the CAN steering-angle factor, signed 16 bit, not yet confirmed on this field: raw values on the Signals page and in the log"
      }
    },
    "dme": {
      "comment": "Intake / fuel values from the engine unit (DME, ecu 18 = 0x12) with UDS 0x22. F4xx = the standard OBD PIDs (F40F = PID 0x0F); a candidate with \"obd\" instead of \"did\" asks for the same PID with OBD service 01 (some engine units refuse the F4xx identifiers with NRC 31). Candidates are tried in order; the first plausible one wins. value = raw * factor + offset (bar / deg C). If a tile says 'not available from this DME', add your engine's BMW-specific DID here. boost: tried in order when the sport display sends no boost (setting 'Boost from'); absolute pressure in kPa, the outside air pressure (baro) is subtracted. boostTarget / boostActual: boost pressure setpoint and actual (absolute kPa, baro subtracted), BMW DIDs first, then OBD PID 0x70; the tile only shows when the target answers. loadTarget / loadActual: requested and actual relative air charge in %. timing: OBD PID 0x0E, degrees before top dead centre. misfire: OBD service 06 monitor results (MID A2 = cylinder 1, A3 = cylinder 2 ...), tid 0C = misfires this driving cycle (0B = average of the last 10 cycles); engine units that only speak UDS are asked 0x22 F6A2... egs: gearbox temperature from the gearbox unit (EGS); give each candidate its \"ecu\".",
